From 970d36036baa903639ca57ed50b1599abe9b7283 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Christopher Owen <3221756+christopherowen@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 8 Nov 2026 12:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] perf(dsv41): per-column pack12 vocab exceptions, row bounds
 and PDL chain on wide GEMM grids

Base: 1107 vLLM patch head 2756478b60b90700b9918b457aeb38657da637b5.

Rationale:
- packed_vocab_projection, packed_vocab_greedy_partials and packed_vocab_markov_greedy_partials in vllm/models/deepseek_v4_1/tilelang/vocab.py added the head's exceptions after the K loop with a tile-wide CSR broadcast: every CTA thread visited every exception of the tile's block_N rows (row_offsets[first] .. row_offsets[first + block_N]) across a T.Parallel(block_M, block_N) loop guarded by `if j == row`. vllm_vocab_apply_row_exceptions / vllm_vocab_apply_row_exceptions_clocal instead has each thread load row_offsets for its 2 MMA fragment columns (c_frag[frag_idx], c_frag[frag_idx + 1]) and accumulate only its own columns' exceptions, in list order.
- _packed_bf16_gemm and packed_bf16_gemm_two in vllm/models/deepseek_v4_1/tilelang/gemm.py called vllm_packed_bf16_filter_exc(..., 0, K, ...) for each row before the K loop, a binary search for col < K over the row's whole exception list (its result is the row's end), and did not begin with pdl.chain(). On grids of _PACKED_WIDE_TILES (32) column tiles or more they now load the bounds with the unconditional vllm_packed_bf16_load_row_bounds and begin with pdl.chain(); narrower grids keep the search and launch as before.
- Register the packed_bf16 split-K, partials and unpack kernels, which already begin with pdl.chain(), in deepseek_v41_pdl_sources.CHAIN.

Round 1 (candidate-51):
The first version also rewrote vllm_vocab_decode_vec16 as an 18-op byte-level __byte_perm SWAR, made vllm_packed_bf16_filter_exc load row_offsets unconditionally, and gave every packed_bf16_gemm and packed_bf16_gemm_two grid the row-bounds load and pdl.chain(). Candidate-51's own mark (sp8, ABBA against candidate-50 without 0778) found it slower on three counts: project_head_greedy_pairs, serving's greedy verification through #997's certified screen, by 0.6-2.6% at TP4 M=97..120 (TP3 likewise); packed_bf16_gemm on 512x10240 at every M (2.5-7.4%) and 128x5120 (2-3%), by isolated kernel time too; and no gain on serving's split-K compressor GEMM, the caller of the changed filter. In-process variants on sp8 (each variant compiled from its own copy of the module) separate the changes:
1. vllm_vocab_decode_vec16: the rewrite is within 0.5% of the base decode in packed_vocab_projection and packed_vocab_greedy_partials at TP4 M=1..128, at the PR's 0.35% exception density and at the 0.015% of a random head's own exceptions; the per-column exceptions carry the whole gain (2.4-3.8x and 1.00-1.25x). The certified screen's vocab_row_thresholds and vocab_packed_refine_partials call the same decode, the only change on that path; in one process the two decodes' screens differ by less than the layer-placement effect seen on identical kernels (up to 7%), so the own mark's cross-image result stands, and this version makes the screen's kernels the base's again (byte-identical SASS) rather than tuning the decode for it.
2. packed_bf16_gemm (two boots): the row-bounds load is 2.3-5.1% slower on 512x10240 and 128x5120 (8 and 2 column tiles of 64, a few CTAs each running a long K loop) and 1.0-6.1% faster on 5120x512 and 4096x1280 (80 and 64 tiles); pdl.chain() is 0.3-1.1% slower on the narrow grids (3.9% at 512x10240 M=256) and 0-2.6% faster on the wide ones.
This version keeps the base's vllm_vocab_decode_vec16, so the screen's kernels are the base's again, and the base's vllm_packed_bf16_filter_exc, so are the split-K and unpack kernels serving runs; it gives the row-bounds load and pdl.chain() to wide grids only (gemm_packed_bf16 and gemm_packed_bf16_two leave CHAIN, as a narrow grid does not wait).

Quality:
Bit-identical (0 ULP): each exception is added to the same FP32 accumulator element, in list order, after the same K loop, and the bounds load returns the bounds the search returned. Round 1: GEMM outputs, projection logits, greedy partial pairs, certified-screen pairs and split-K outputs are equal across both arms, every boot and both TILE_CONFIGS[128] variants.

Tests:
- pytest tests/kernels/quantization/test_deepseek_v41_tilelang_vocab.py tests/kernels/quantization/test_deepseek_v41_tilelang_linear.py tests/kernels/test_deepseek_v41_tilelang_embedding.py tests/kernels/test_deepseek_v41_tilelang_pdl.py (274 passed across 2 boots; PDL sources: 449 kernels launched, 0 violations).
- Round 1: test_packed_bf16_gemm_wide_and_narrow_grids_exact: on wide grids, and only there, the kernel source waits and loads row bounds; outputs equal bf16_gemm / bf16_gemm_two bit for bit on both. The four files on candidate-51's corrected tree with the PDL sources plugin: 287 passed on each of two container runs (PDL sources: 500 and 490 kernels launched, 0 violations).

Upstream status: local DeepSeek-V4.1 SM121 TileLang packed BF16 kernel tuning.
